{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 132, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing the 0->3 edge often leaves only edge 5 or nothing feeding the output, collapsing accuracy (exps 14,18,20,22 vs 13,17,21)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is none, edge 3 may be the only remaining input to node 3, so deleting it disconnects the cell (exps 14,18,20,22)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where none existed helps more than replacing an existing conv/pool on the 0->3 edge (exps 41,46,47,48 vs 42,43,44)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 4, removing edge 5 strips most or all paths into the output node (exps 79,80 vs 77)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the final edge with a 3x3 conv adds substantial capacity on the main path (exps 7,8,98)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the input-output skip is missing, a skip on 1->3 supplies the residual path that deep conv cells need (exp 92 vs 91)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip into the output compensates for the missing 0->3 residual, improving trainability (exp 90 vs 89)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 edge, deleting edge 4 removes one of only two remaining routes into the output (exp 82 vs 81)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "